UID:welcome-day-fall-2026-orientation@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Welcome Day - Fall 2026 Orientation\n\nAll new students are in
 vited to Welcome Day\, where we will kick off the academic year. Meet your
  peers\, meet our staff\, learn about our services and supports\, and conn
 ect with the wider neighbourhood and community. 8:30 to 9:30 a.m. Check in
  at the Welcome Tent to get your Welcome Kit\, team button and wristband f
 or refreshments and join your team 9:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. Welcome remarks
 \, meet your peers and join in the fun! Meet your Team Captains\, get your
  team pin\, and meet other students from your program and faculty! Collect
  your free Welcome Kit Welcome Remarks with greetings from Indigenous Elde
 r Liz Osawamick\, President & Vice-Chancellor Ana Serrano\, Vice-Provost\,
  Students & International\, Deanne Fisher and your Student Union Check out
  our Student Services Expo where you can meet our staff and learn about ou
 r many supports and resources Participate in creative activities\, insider
  panel discussions\, and chances to win prizes! 12:30 to 4 p.m. OCAD U's a
 nnual Community Fair featuring: The Above Ground Art Supplies Art Material
 s Fair Student clubs and campus organizations\, Special guest hosts from O
 CAD U LiVE Enjoy refreshments (while supplies last)\, samples\, give-aways
 \, and so much more! 2 to 3 p.m. International Student Coffee Break Levels
  5 and 6\, 230 Richmond St. West Quiet Space: Need to get away from the no
 ise and action of Welcome Day! for a little break\, meditation\, or quiet 
 contemplation? The Student Lounge (MCA 274\, Level 2\, 100 McCaul St.) has
  been designated as Quiet Space during orientation. Another option is our 
 Multi-faith Room (MCA 657\, Level 6\, 100 McCaul St.). For more informatio
 n\, visit ocadu.ca/orientation OCAD U strives to provide inclusive and acc
 essible opportunities for the entire OCAD U community to participate fully
 . If you require any type of accommodation to participate in this activity
 \, please let us know: campuslife@ocadu.ca Photography Notice: Please be a
 dvised that OCAD U events may be documented through photographs and video.
  These images may be used by the University for promotional\, advertising\
 , educational\, and archival purposes. By attending the event\, you acknow
 ledge that photography and videography may occur. If you prefer not to be 
 featured in identifiable photographs or video recordings\, please speak wi
 th a member of the event team upon arrival. We will make reasonable effort
 s to accommodate your request\; however\, due to the nature and size of th
 e event\, we cannot guarantee that you will not appear incidentally in cro
 wd images or recordings.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street 100 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/welcome-day-fall-2026-orie
 ntation
